.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt PCH_PIC 4 loongarch64
.Os
.\" .Nm loongarch64/pch_pic
.Sh NAME
.Nm pch_pic
.Nd Loongson platform controller hub interrupt controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
This driver is a standard part of the LoongArch kernel.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides support for the interrupt controller in the Loongson
platform controller hub.
It manages up to 64 interrupt inputs and routes them to
.Xr eioic 4 .
The driver configures interrupt masking, trigger mode, and polarity,
and acknowledges interrupts from platform devices, including PCI INTx.
.Pp
On ACPI systems the controller is instantiated by the platform nexus
and maps global system interrupts using the PCH interrupt controller
entry in the Multiple APIC Description Table (MADT).
When ACPI is absent, it attaches to a flattened device tree node with
the compatible string
.Qq loongson,pch-pic-1.0 .
The device tree must provide the controller's register range and the
.Qq loongson,pic-base-vec
property specifying its starting EIOINTC vector.
.Pp
No driver-specific kernel configuration directive is required.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr cpuic 4 ,
.Xr eioic 4 ,
.Xr fdt 4 ,
.Xr pci 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver was added in the LoongArch port of
.Fx 16.0 .
